#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068917 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068569 :question/id #uuid "234c7a86-037c-5316-9419-14db90d1da60" :question/math-academy-id "e-466" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x^2 \\sec^2\\left(x^3-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u = x^3 - \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} u}{\\textrm{d}x } = 3x^2 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u = x^2\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡({x}^{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d359337c-4ec2-5100-bdac-d0858619db3b" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678343 :question-generator/id #uuid "61eead49-e468-5998-bf51-233e22781506" :question-generator/script "generators/bd/bd6f965372c18c7ca5575189c1bd6e450b5dc291813e8c02909a532a277e2e78/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069045 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91d866f1-e720-5398-a46e-0722090f6821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos (x^{2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065704} {:answer/id #uuid "c75da138-5eaf-58e3-a55c-12f0301a6fde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\cos (x^{2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065705} {:answer/id #uuid "ef04e350-3350-5a0b-a549-5f78e588537b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\cos (x^{2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065706} {:answer/id #uuid "3a105d51-4ff7-5170-