stion/id #uuid "84f073b5-e3b1-59e9-a055-a6e9dcf4b5cf" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=x^{2}$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int 2 x \\cos{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^{2}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2 x.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2 x \\cos{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "796b20c7-6752-54be-9ba7-0e02d42d6849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{1}{x} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "796b20c7-6752-54be-9ba7-0e02d42d6849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{1}{x} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678290} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5b81ad-c73c-5093-8f9f-232ea653d45b" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678277}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "905bff24-82d3-5866-9044-a52ed8f0e8c4" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{1}{x} \\right)}}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{1}{x}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{x^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{2 \\cos{\\left(\\frac{1}{x} \\right)}}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-2\\left(\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n-2\\left(\\int \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- 2 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- 2 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{1}{x} \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678297 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5c877b4-db6b-5042-9f8f-62cde24c9fcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sec{\\left(x^{3} + 2 \\right)}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5c877b4-db6b-5042-9f8f-62cde24c9fcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sec{\\left(x^{3} + 2 \\right)}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678304} :answer-field/id #uuid "432e7c05-7724-598e-814b-fb2c94effcd6" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678262}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9566aff7-b976-5c0a-85c3-d7d41083e7b1" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int x^{2} \\tan{\\left(x^{3} + 2 \\right)} \\sec{\\left(x^{3} + 2 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sec{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^{3} + 2$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3 x^{2}.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int x^{2} \\tan{\\left(x^{3} + 2 \\right)} \\sec{\\left(x^{3} + 2 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{\\sec{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sec{\\left(x^{3} + 2 \\right)}}{3}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678303 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d87ae77-06b9-5d22-994c-0dd36d086d92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\csc{\\left(x^{2} + 2 \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d87ae77-06b9-5d22-994c-0dd36d086d92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\csc{\\left(x^{2} + 2 \\right)}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678286} :answer-field/id #uuid "b21ed25c-933f-522c-a404-61fadc00d605" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678307}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4406e92-3fdf-528c-bc71-97d93112204f" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 3 x \\cot{\\left(x^{2} + 2 \\right)} \\csc{\\left(x^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^{2} + 2$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2 x.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 3 x \\cot{\\left(x^{2} + 2 \\right)} \\csc{\\left(x^{2} + 2 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{3 \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{3 \\csc{\\left(x^{2} + 2 \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f91cf734-d9a2-5c15-ba32-f6d129eb976d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\sec{\\left(\\frac{1}{x + 1} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f91cf734-d9a2-5c15-ba32-f6d129eb976d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\sec{\\left(\\frac{1}{x + 1} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678338} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb33753b-15c2-5041-9331-0cf5c84e60bc" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678334}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b24398ca-99b9-5a39-a042-a9b6d791af93" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3 \\tan{\\left(\\frac{1}{x + 1} \\right)} \\sec{\\left(\\frac{1}{x + 1} \\right)}}{\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\sec{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{1}{x + 1}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{3 \\tan{\\left(\\frac{1}{x + 1} \\right)} \\sec{\\left(\\frac{1}{x + 1} \\right)}}{\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-3\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n-3\\left(\\int \\tan{\\left(u \\right)} \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- 3 \\sec{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- 3 \\sec{\\left(\\frac{1}{x + 1} \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10306567-3786-5bb6-b48a-264df6f8c19c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678246} {:answer/id #uuid "1a6b9c1a-750b-5917-bf9b-72064d5ab3dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678248} {:answer/id #uuid "5891f849-cdc9-5a96-9500-7ed3b726bd69" :answer/type {:db/