left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{1}{x + 1}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{3 \\sec^{2}{\\left(\\frac{1}{x + 1} \\right)}}{\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-3\\left(\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n-3\\left(\\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- 3 \\tan{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- 3 \\tan{\\left(\\frac{1}{x + 1} \\right)}+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678342 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74dfefa1-40e2-5015-9e25-907b347524d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678287} {:answer/id #uuid "a999c23f-1cc7-5eb8-8800-723fdf9fc145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678305} {:answer/id #uuid "d0203d56-ba3d-5688-a894-ced5460e75fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678319} {:answer/id #uuid "d024d229-84b9-59b9-8437-8889ef040537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678320} {:answer/id #uuid "d938ae3b-c317-58e2-9249-1a13d0600ae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d938ae3b-c317-58e2-9249-1a13d0600ae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678327} :answer-field/id #uuid "be6e3500-44ed-5337-8838-0adbdc9605bb" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678315}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fda80108-f3cb-5d6f-be8c-842c99ce457f" :question/problem "Use the substitution $u=x^{3}$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int 2 x^{2} \\cot{\\left(x^{3} \\right)} \\csc{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=x^{3}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3 x^{2}.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2 x^{2} \\cot{\\left(x^{3} \\right)} \\csc{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Products Containing Trigonometric Functions Using Substitution"}]}
